Specification TransactionRegister

Description The transaction register of one account: what each line shows, what
Description order the lines are in, and what the running balance means.
Details
Details A register is always a view of one account. Every line of it is one
Details posting to that account, with the other side of the transaction
Details summarised in the Category column. A transaction with four postings
Details appears once in each of the four registers, showing a different
Details amount and a different category each time, and it is the same
Details transaction.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A line of the register
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes RegisterLine
Description One line as it appears on screen.
Details Payment and Deposit are headed differently for different account types;
Details see the column heading rule below. Balance is the running balance after
Details this line.
| Attribute | Type           | Default    |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |            |
| Date      | Date           | 2024-01-01 |
| CheckNo   | CheckNumber    | none       |
| Payee     | PayeeName      | none       |
| Category  | Text           | none       |
| Memo      | Text           | none       |
| Payment   | Money          | 0.00       |
| Deposit   | Money          | 0.00       |
| Cleared   | ClearedStatus  | Uncleared  |
| Balance   | Money          | 0.00       |

Scenario A register of simple transactions
Description The Category column holds the other account of the transaction. The
Description running balance is the balance of this account after each line.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Income:Salary      | Income  | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account            | Amount   |
| T1  | 2024-01-01 | Acme Payroll  | Assets:Checking    | 3000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-01 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary      | -3000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking    | -45.00   |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 45.00    |
| T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shell         | Assets:Checking    | -52.00   |
| T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 52.00    |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Category           | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T1  | 2024-01-01 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary      | 0.00    | 3000.00 | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 45.00   | 0.00    | 2955.00 |
| T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 52.00   | 0.00    | 2903.00 |

Scenario The same transaction seen from the other account
Description T2 above, in the register of the category rather than the bank. The
Description amount is on the other side and the category column names the bank.
Description Nothing was stored twice to make this possible.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path               |
| Expenses:Groceries |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Category        | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking | 0.00    | 45.00   | 45.00   |
# In an Expense register the money arriving is what was spent, so it falls in
# the Deposit column. The column heading rule below gives it a better name.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Column headings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule What the two amount columns are called
Description The register is read as a statement of the account it is open on, so
Description the headings are the words that account uses.
Examples: ColumnHeadings
| AccountType | OutColumn | InColumn | Notes                             |
| Bank        | Payment   | Deposit  |                                   |
| Cash        | Spend     | Receive  |                                   |
| CreditCard  | Charge    | Payment  | A payment reduces what is owed    |
| Liability   | Increase  | Payment  |                                   |
| Asset       | Decrease  | Increase |                                   |
| Investment  | Payment   | Deposit  | Of the cash side; see Investments |
| Expense     | Refund    | Spent    | Money arriving here was spent     |
| Income      | Earned    | Returned |                                   |
| Equity      | Decrease  | Increase |                                   |

Attributes ColumnHeadings
| Attribute   | Type        | Default |
| AccountType | AccountType | Bank    |
| OutColumn   | Text        |         |
| InColumn    | Text        |         |
| Notes       | String      | none    |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The running balance
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule The running balance uses the display sign of the account
Description A credit card register shows what is owed, growing as it is charged,
Description because that is what the statement shows. See the display sign rule
Description in Accounts.
Examples: RunningBalanceSign
| AccountType | PostingAmount | BalanceShown | Notes                      |
| Bank        | -45.00        | -45.00       | Money left the account     |
| CreditCard  | -45.00        | 45.00        | A charge; 45.00 is owed    |
| CreditCard  | 300.00        | -300.00      | A payment, on its own      |
| Income      | -3000.00      | 3000.00      | Earned                     |

Attributes RunningBalanceSign
| Attribute     | Type        | Default |
| AccountType   | AccountType | Bank    |
| PostingAmount | Money       | 0.00    |
| BalanceShown  | Money       | 0.00    |
| Notes         | String      | none    |

Scenario A credit card register shows a growing balance owed
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path              | Type       | Placeholder |
| Liabilities:Visa  | CreditCard | false       |
| Assets:Checking   | Bank       | false       |
| Expenses:Shopping | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Dining   | Expense    | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee     | Account           | Amount  |
| T1  | 2024-03-02 | Amazon    | Liabilities:Visa  | -89.99  |
| T1  | 2024-03-02 | Amazon    | Expenses:Shopping | 89.99   |
| T2  | 2024-03-09 | The Cafe  | Liabilities:Visa  | -18.50  |
| T2  | 2024-03-09 | The Cafe  | Expenses:Dining   | 18.50   |
| T3  | 2024-03-25 | Visa      | Liabilities:Visa  | 100.00  |
| T3  | 2024-03-25 | Visa      | Assets:Checking   | -100.00 |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path             |
| Liabilities:Visa |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee    | Category          | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T1  | 2024-03-02 | Amazon   | Expenses:Shopping | 89.99   | 0.00    | 89.99   |
| T2  | 2024-03-09 | The Cafe | Expenses:Dining   | 18.50   | 0.00    | 108.49  |
| T3  | 2024-03-25 | Visa     | Assets:Checking   | 0.00    | 100.00  | 8.49    |
# Payment here is headed Charge, and Deposit is headed Payment.

BusinessRule What order the register is in
Description By date, and within a date by the order the transactions were entered.
Details Entry order is used for the tie rather than amount or payee because it
Details is stable: reopening the file, or importing more, never reshuffles
Details lines that are already there, so the running balance against a line
Details does not change under the user.
Examples: RegisterOrder
| Date       | EntrySeq | Position | Notes                              |
| 2024-01-15 | 2        | 1        | Earliest date first                |
| 2024-01-20 | 1        | 2        | Entered first, dated later         |
| 2024-01-20 | 3        | 3        | Same date, entered after           |
| 2024-01-20 | 4        | 4        |                                    |

Attributes RegisterOrder
| Attribute | Type    | Default    |
| Date      | Date    | 2024-01-01 |
| EntrySeq  | Integer | 0          |
| Position  | Integer | 0          |
| Notes     | String  | none       |

Scenario Two transactions on one date keep the order they were entered in
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given postings in entry order are : SequencedPostingRow
| EntrySeq | Ref | Date       | Payee | Account            | Amount |
| 1        | T1  | 2024-01-20 | Shop A | Assets:Checking   | -10.00 |
| 1        | T1  | 2024-01-20 | Shop A | Expenses:Groceries | 10.00 |
| 2        | T2  | 2024-01-15 | Shop B | Assets:Checking   | -20.00 |
| 2        | T2  | 2024-01-15 | Shop B | Expenses:Groceries | 20.00 |
| 3        | T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shop C | Assets:Checking   | -30.00 |
| 3        | T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shop C | Expenses:Groceries | 30.00 |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee  | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Shop B | 20.00   | 0.00    | -20.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-20 | Shop A | 10.00   | 0.00    | -30.00  |
| T3  | 2024-01-20 | Shop C | 30.00   | 0.00    | -60.00  |

Attributes SequencedPostingRow
| Attribute | Type           | Default    |
| EntrySeq  | Integer        | 0          |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |            |
| Date      | Date           | 2024-01-01 |
| Payee     | PayeeName      | none       |
| Account   | AccountPath    |            |
| Amount    | Money          | 0.00       |

Scenario Sorting the register by another column hides the running balance
Description A running balance down a list that is not in date order is a column
Description of meaningless numbers. Sorting by payee is useful for finding
Description something, so it is allowed, and the balance column is emptied
Description rather than filled with figures that do not add up.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings in entry order are as previous
When register sorted by : SortBy
| Column |
| Payee  |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Payee  | Balance |
| T1  | Shop A | 0.00    |
| T2  | Shop B | 0.00    |
| T3  | Shop C | 0.00    |
Then running balance is shown : BalanceColumnState Vertical
| Shown  | false                                  |
| Reason | The register is not in date order      |

DataType SortColumn
Description Which column the register is sorted by.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value   | Notes                                  |
| Date    | The default, and the only one that adds up |
| Payee   |                                        |
| Category |                                       |
| Amount  |                                        |
| CheckNo |                                        |
| Cleared |                                        |

Attributes BalanceColumnState
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Shown     | Boolean | true    |
| Reason    | Text    | none    |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Splits in the register
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario A split shows as Split in the category column
Description There is no one category to show, so the column says so, and the
Description line can be expanded to see the parts.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                      | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking           | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Home:Maintenance | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Home:Garden      | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs     | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee      | Account                   | Amount  | Memo         |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | Assets:Checking           | -184.50 | none         |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | Expenses:Home:Maintenance | 100.00  | Paint        |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | Expenses:Home:Garden      | 54.50   | Compost      |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | Expenses:Auto:Repairs     | 30.00   | Wiper blades |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee      | Category | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | --Split-- | 184.50 | 0.00    | -184.50 |

Scenario An expanded split shows its lines beneath
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When line expanded : TransactionSelect
| Ref |
| T1  |
Then split lines shown are : SplitLineShown
| Category                  | Amount | Memo         |
| Expenses:Home:Maintenance | 100.00 | Paint        |
| Expenses:Home:Garden      | 54.50  | Compost      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs     | 30.00  | Wiper blades |

Attributes SplitLineShown
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Category  | AccountPath |         |
| Amount    | Money       | 0.00    |
| Memo      | Text        | none    |

Scenario A split seen from one of its category registers shows only its own line
Description The register of Expenses:Home:Garden shows 54.50, not 184.50, and
Description names the bank account as the category. The other legs of the split
Description are not its business.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path                 |
| Expenses:Home:Garden |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine
| Ref | Date       | Payee      | Category        | Memo    | Payment | Deposit | Balance |
| T1  | 2024-04-02 | Home Depot | Assets:Checking | Compost | 0.00    | 54.50   | 54.50   |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dates in the future, and over many years
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario A future-dated transaction appears at the end, below a marker
Description A check written today and dated next month belongs in the register,
Description and it must not be mistaken for money already gone. The balance as
Description at today is shown on the marker line.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee  | Account            | Amount  |
| T1  | 2024-05-01 | Shop A | Assets:Checking    | 1000.00 |
| T1  | 2024-05-01 | Shop A | Expenses:Groceries | -1000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-05-10 | Shop B | Assets:Checking    | -40.00  |
| T2  | 2024-05-10 | Shop B | Expenses:Groceries | 40.00   |
| T3  | 2024-06-01 | Shop C | Assets:Checking    | -60.00  |
| T3  | 2024-06-01 | Shop C | Expenses:Groceries | 60.00   |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Balance |
| T1  | 2024-05-01 | 1000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-05-10 | 960.00  |
| T3  | 2024-06-01 | 900.00  |
Then today marker is : TodayMarker Vertical
| AfterRef       | T2         |
| BalanceToday   | 960.00     |
| FutureCount    | 1          |
| FutureTotal    | -60.00     |

Attributes Today
| Attribute | Type | Default    |
| Date      | Date | 2024-05-15 |

Attributes TodayMarker
| Attribute     | Type           | Default |
| AfterRef      | TransactionRef | none    |
| BalanceToday  | Money          | 0.00    |
| FutureCount   | Integer        | 0       |
| FutureTotal   | Money          | 0.00    |

Scenario The register opens on the most recent transactions
Description Twenty years of history is tens of thousands of lines. Opening at
Description the top would mean scrolling through 2005 to reach this month.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path            | Type | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking | Bank | false       |
Given the register holds : RegisterExtent Vertical
| FirstDate | 2005-01-01 |
| LastDate  | 2026-09-30 |
| LineCount | 41238      |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then register view is : RegisterView Vertical
| ScrolledTo   | 2026-09-30 |
| SelectedLine | last       |
| LinesLoaded  | 41238      |

Attributes RegisterExtent
| Attribute | Type    | Default    |
| FirstDate | Date    | 2005-01-01 |
| LastDate  | Date    | 2026-09-30 |
| LineCount | Integer | 0          |

Attributes RegisterView
| Attribute    | Type | Default    |
| ScrolledTo   | Date | 2026-09-30 |
| SelectedLine | Text | last       |
| LinesLoaded  | Integer | 0       |

Scenario A date filter narrows the register without changing the balance
Description The running balance shown against a line is the balance of the
Description account, not of the filtered list. A line that reads 2,903.00 in
Description the unfiltered register reads 2,903.00 when only January is shown,
Description because that is what the account held on that day.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee  | Account            | Amount  |
| T1  | 2023-12-20 | Shop A | Assets:Checking    | 1000.00 |
| T1  | 2023-12-20 | Shop A | Expenses:Groceries | -1000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Shop B | Assets:Checking    | -45.00  |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | Shop B | Expenses:Groceries | 45.00   |
| T3  | 2024-02-20 | Shop C | Assets:Checking    | -52.00  |
| T3  | 2024-02-20 | Shop C | Expenses:Groceries | 52.00   |
When register filtered to dates : DateRange Vertical
| From | 2024-01-01 |
| To   | 2024-01-31 |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Balance |
| T2  | 2024-01-15 | 955.00  |
Then opening balance line is : OpeningLine Vertical
| AsAt    | 2023-12-31 |
| Balance | 1000.00    |

Attributes DateRange
| Attribute | Type | Default    |
| From      | Date | 2024-01-01 |
| To        | Date | 2024-12-31 |

Attributes OpeningLine
| Attribute | Type  | Default    |
| AsAt      | Date  | 2024-01-01 |
| Balance   | Money | 0.00       |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Finding things
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario Searching the register matches payee, memo, category and amount
Description One search box, because a user looking for something does not want
Description to decide first which field it is in.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account            | Amount | Memo          |
| T1  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking    | -45.00 | weekly shop   |
| T1  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 45.00  | none          |
| T2  | 2024-01-20 | Shell         | Assets:Checking    | -52.00 | shop on route |
| T2  | 2024-01-20 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 52.00  | none          |
When register searched for : SearchTerm
| Term |
| shop |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Payee         |
| T1  | Harris Teeter |
| T2  | Shell         |
# T1 matches on its memo, T2 on its memo as well. Both are offered; the
# search does not rank.

DataType SearchText
Description What was typed into the search box.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value | IsValid | Notes                        |
| shop  | true    |                              |
| 45.00 | true    | An amount is searched for too |
|       | true    | Empty clears the search      |

Scenario Searching for an amount matches either column
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When register searched for : SearchTerm
| Term  |
| 52.00 |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Payee |
| T2  | Shell |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entering on the blank line
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario The blank line at the end takes the next transaction
Description The register ends in an empty line dated today. Filling it in and
Description leaving the line commits the transaction, as in Transactions.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then blank line is : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Date       | Payee | Payment | Deposit |
| 2024-05-15 | none  | 0.00    | 0.00    |

Scenario Leaving a part-filled blank line with no amount discards it
Description A payee typed and then thought better of does not become a zero
Description transaction.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given today is as previous
When blank line filled : RegisterLine Vertical CompareOnly
| Payee | Harris Teeter |
When blank line left
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref |
# No rows: nothing was committed.
